  "title": "Bounded Worker-Pool Map",
  "language": "python",
  "difficulty": "core",
  "estimatedMinutes": 35,
  "instructions": "Implement `bounded_map(func, items, *, workers, queue_size=None)` in `pipeline.py`. A fixed pool of `workers` tasks consumes a bounded `asyncio.Queue` that a producer fills lazily from `items`, so memory stays bounded for any iterable. Return results in input order, stop workers with one `None` sentinel each, and make the first failure cancel everything without deadlocking.",
